# Python style

- Python 3.12+ style: `X | None`, dataclasses or Pydantic, type hints on public functions.
- No module-level mutable "active profile". Pass profile objects into services.
- Do not blindly unpack profile fields into API calls; omit unsupported params; fail locally on contradictions.
- Log profile name, model, and non-secret effective params. Never log secrets or full DB rows.
- Keep prompts named and versionable; do not bury them in route handlers once they exist.
- Format/lint with ruff when the project has it. Tests via `uv run pytest`.
